  "card": "This pull request passes Bitcoin Core's compiler hardening flags to the embedded libsecp256k1 build by separating them into a reusable CMake interface target. The secp256k1 subtree was previously built without flags such as stack protection and control-flow protection. Because linkers require all linked object files to support control-flow integrity to mark the binary as protected, secp256k1 objects prevented the final executable from having hardware-assisted control-flow protection notes on systems like AArch64 Linux. On Ubuntu 26.04 with GCC 15, this change restores the binary's AArch64 BTI, PAC, and GCS feature markers.",
